<!--
  lastmod is the only field here Google actually reads - it ignores changefreq
  and priority entirely, and has said so for years. They are kept because Bing
  and Yandex still look at them.

  Set lastmod to the date the page's CONTENT really changed, never the build
  date: a sitemap that claims every page changed on every deploy teaches the
  crawler to stop trusting the field. The two legal pages carry their own
  "Son güncelleme" date from the page body for exactly that reason.

  prerender.test.ts fails the build if a URL listed here is not prerendered:
  /privacy and /terms sat in this file for months while serving the homepage's
  title, H1 and canonical="/" to anything that does not run JS.
-->
